> Selected results and weak reconstruction controls

Both selected checkpoints are epoch3. Test NLL beta1/4 is239.924/260.339 nats/image;
KL29.775/11.192 and common NLL+KL269.699/271.531. The beta4 weighted objective is305.107,
which should not be compared with beta1's269.699 as a common model-selection score.
The fitting-only mean has pixel MSE0.04855, better than either decode(mu) reconstruction.
This short run trades reconstruction against KL and does not demonstrate a useful disentangled
representation. Epoch-zero test scores are recorded as controls, not candidates for selection.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/beta_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (int beta : {1, 4}) {
    std::vector<double> epoch, criterion;
    std::ifstream       f("build/beta_vae/beta" + std::to_string(beta) + "/history.tsv");
    std::string         line;
    std::getline(f, line);
    while (std::getline(f, line)) {
      std::istringstream r(line);
      double             e, fit, nll, kl, common, weighted;
      r >> e >> fit >> nll >> kl >> common >> weighted;
      epoch.push_back(e);
      criterion.push_back(common);
    }
    chart.lines(
        epoch,
        criterion,
        "beta" + std::to_string(beta),
        beta == 1 ? dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235} : dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38},
        2);
  }
  chart.title("Common four-draw validation criterion")
      .x_label("completed epoch")
      .y_label("NLL + KL / nats per image")
      .save_svg("build/beta_learning.svg");
}
