> Prior decoder probabilities and one-coordinate traversals

Both priors use exactly the same20 standard-normal four-coordinate codes. These images are
sigmoid decoder probabilities, not sampled Bernoulli pixels. Traversals vary one coordinate
around the fitting-only mean of mu by−2,−1.5,…,2, holding the other coordinates fixed.
Changing outputs along an axis does not establish that the axis encodes a single semantic factor.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/beta_prior.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
