> Fitting-only factor recovery diagnostics

After representation training and checkpoint selection, the core standardizes latent means
using210 fitting rows (population std, floor1e-8) and centers fitting factor targets. All-axis
ridge solves (XᵀX+.001I)C=XᵀY in Float64. A separate single-axis probe selects the largest
absolute **fitting** Pearson correlation, with lower-index ties, then fits a slope with the same
ridge penalty. Each test prediction adds the fitting target mean. Test labels are used only for
heldout R² and diagnostic correlations; they cannot select axes, scale features or select checkpoints.

R²=1−SSE/∑(testtarget−testmean)² retains negative values. Treating shape/size indices as
numeric targets is a linear recovery diagnostic, not classification accuracy. The thirteen-array
factor_probes.npz also records latent means/std, population variance, per-unit fitting KL,
fitting/test correlations, coefficients, selected axes and both prediction matrices. Recovery
from all axes can coexist with strongly mixed axes. These are not MIG/DCI or the paper's
classifier-based disentanglement score; this three-epoch single-seed lattice run supports no
claim of general disentanglement.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/beta_probes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto chart  = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  std::print(
      "| beta | factor | selected axis | single-axis R2 | ridge R2 |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  const char* names[] = {"shape", "size", "x", "y"};
  for (int b : {1, 4}) {
    std::vector<double>              factor;
    std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> d;
    for (const auto& [k, v] :
         n::load_npz("build/beta_vae/beta" + std::to_string(b) + "/factor_probes.npz"))
      d.emplace(k, v);
    const auto axes   = d.at("best_axis_by_fit").to_vector<int>();
    const auto ridge  = d.at("ridge_r2").to_vector<double>(),
               single = d.at("single_r2").to_vector<double>();
    for (int j = 0; j < 4; ++j) {
      factor.push_back(j + (b == 1 ? -.05 : .05));
      std::print("|{}|{}|{}|{:.6f}|{:.6f}|\n", b, names[j], axes[j], single[j], ridge[j]);
    }
    chart.points(
        factor,
        ridge,
        "beta" + std::to_string(b),
        b == 1 ? dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235} : dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38},
        6);
  }
  chart.title("Fitting-only linear factor probes / small horizontal display offset")
      .x_label("factor: 0 shape /1 size /2 x /3 y")
      .y_label("test ridge R2")
      .save_svg("build/beta_probes.svg");
}
