> Reuse and evidence

The canonical reusable operations are models::GaussianReparameterize, DiagonalGaussianKl,
GaussianVaeDecode, BetaVariationalAutoencoder and LatentFactorDiagnostics. Python and R
expose the same C++ operations through generated bindings. This report contains the complete
editable C++ programs, including both training loops through the visible Train function;
no legacy example header or external checkout is required. Source-compatible helpers remain
thin adapters while later VAE examples still depend on them.

The migration verifies every array of all30 original NPZ archives, both batch-order TSVs and
all validation-history values. Selected checkpoints, initial forward values, first gradients,
first updates, all epochs, posterior banks, priors, traversals and factor probes remain available
under build/beta_vae. Fixed-noise repeats, target-free decoding, epsilon-zero posterior means,
noise-independent heads, single/batch parity and immutable inference are executed checks.
